    "created_at": "2026-10-27T16:47:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-27T16:47:59Z",
    "body": "https://wpt.fyi/results/html/browsers/the-window-object/window-reuse.tentative.html\n\nI believe browsers currently only reuse the inner window if the navigable was immediately navigated to a non-`about:blank` URI. But browsers differ on what properties they reset on the window element, like the navigator or custom element registry.\n\nRelevant parts of Gecko's implementation are `nsGlobalWindowOuter::WouldReuseInnerWindow` and [these lines](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/d9098b3e11c2fbc2b2d84e53a3c784814cbdab3e/dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp#2484-2501) in `SetNewDocument`.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
